#{[17592186433682 #edb/ref 1080 "(R-{A}^{T}A)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433682 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433682 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8091e143-1c62-5487-9984-834771a83882" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6bf75937-c3db-5f40-8e20-ee3efbdf6a43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139766" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,x={Q}^{T}\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the matrix equation above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ What is the missing part of the equation?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "553d1e63-f638-55c5-a882-d8b6a7339c64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ R\\,\\,x & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part of the equation is $R.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
